DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     The pptthhrreeaadd__rrwwlloocckk__wwrrlloocckk() function blocks until a write lock can be ac‐
     quired against _l_o_c_k.  The pptthhrreeaadd__rrwwlloocckk__ttrryywwrrlloocckk() function performs
     the same action, but does not block if the lock cannot be immediately ob‐
     tained.

     The results are undefined if the calling thread already holds the lock at
     the time the call is made.

IIMMPPLLEEMMEENNTTAATTIIOONN NNOOTTEESS
     To prevent writer starvation, writers are favored over readers.

RREETTUURRNN VVAALLUUEESS
     If successful, the pptthhrreeaadd__rrwwlloocckk__wwrrlloocckk() and pptthhrreeaadd__rrwwlloocckk__ttrryywwrrlloocckk()
     functions will return zero.  Otherwise an error number will be returned
     to indicate the error.

EERRRROORRSS
     The pptthhrreeaadd__rrwwlloocckk__ttrryywwrrlloocckk() function will fail if:

     [EBUSY]            The calling thread is not able to acquire the lock
                        without blocking.

     The pptthhrreeaadd__rrwwlloocckk__wwrrlloocckk() and pptthhrreeaadd__rrwwlloocckk__ttrryywwrrlloocckk() functions may
     fail if:

     [EDEADLK]          The calling thread already owns the read/write lock
                        (for reading or writing).

     [EINVAL]           The value specified by _l_o_c_k is invalid.

     [ENOMEM]           Insufficient memory exists to initialize the lock (ap‐
                        plies to statically initialized locks only).

